    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0064" n="1528" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg1528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 60 D 137: Files of the National Advisory
                    Council on International Monetary and Financial Problems</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Snyder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d23-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1951-04-05">April 5, 1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Philippine Congress on March 23, 1951, enacted for a period of two years a
                    tax of 17% on sales of foreign exchange<anchor n="2" xml:id="d23-f2"/> for
                    certain purposes. This enactment has been approved by President Quirino. The
                    submission of this legislation for your approval is required under Article V of
                    the Executive Agreement of July 4, 1946, between the United States and the
                    Republic of the Philippines regarding the value, convertibility and
                    transferability of Philippine currency in relation to the currency of the United
                        States.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d23-f3"/> Consistent with the requirement of
                    the Executive Agreement, a communication<anchor n="4" xml:id="d23-f4"/> has been
                    received by the Secretary of State from the Philippine Ambassador to the United
                    States, the Honorable Joaquin M. Elizalde, requesting that your agreement be
                    given to the imposition of this tax by his Government.</p>
                <p>The enactment of the tax measure referred to is in accord with the
                    recommendations of the Economic Survey Mission to the Philippines, <pb
                        facs="0065" n="1529" xml:id="pg1529"/> and is a step taken in implementation
                    of the agreement of November 14, 1950, between your representative, Mr. William
                    C. Foster, and President Quirino. Accordingly, the National Advisory Council
                    recommends that your approval thereof be given. There is attached for this
                    purpose a statement<anchor n="5" xml:id="d23-f5"/> for your signature agreeing
                    to the imposition of this tax.</p>
                <p>Notification of your approval will be given to the Philippine Government by the
                    Secretary of State.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John</hi> W. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Snyder</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chairman</hi>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">National Advisory Council on International Monetary and
                        Financial Problems</hi><anchor n="6" xml:id="d23-f6"/>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d23-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d23-f1-content">
                <p>The source text is attachment B to NAC Document No. 1121, April 10.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d23-f2" n="2" xml:id="d23-f2-content">
                <p>Signed by President Quirino on March 28.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d23-f3" n="3" xml:id="d23-f3-content">
                <p>For text of the Agreement concerning trade and related matters, signed at Manila
                    July 4, 1946, see 61 Stat. (pt. 3) 2611.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d23-f4" n="4" xml:id="d23-f4-content">
                <p>Of April 2, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d23-f5" n="5" xml:id="d23-f5-content">
                <p>Not printed. President Truman signed it April 6.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d23-f6" n="6" xml:id="d23-f6-content">
                <p>Mr. Snyder held this post <hi rendition="#italic">ex officio</hi> as Secretary of
                    the Treasury.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
